        "original_id": "02732057-e8b6-5cc0-8752-08fef58eb507",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: 43d Air Mobility Operations Group, 43d Aeromedical Evacuation Squadron, Air Mobility Command, USAF Expeditionary Center, United States Army\n- Places: Pope Field, Pope Army Air Field, Fort Bragg, North Carolina, Pope AFB\n\nFacts:\n- Fort Bragg, North Carolina, is a United States Army military installation and is the world's largest military installation by population, with more than 50,000 active duty personnel.\n- The 43d Air Mobility Operations Group is an active duty air mobility unit located at Pope Field in Fort Bragg, North Carolina.\n- Pope Field was formerly called Pope AFB.\n- The 43d Air Mobility Operations Group is part of the Air Mobility Command USAF Expeditionary Center.\n- The 43d Aeromedical Evacuation Squadron is part of the 43d Air Mobility Operations Group at Pope Army Air Field, North Carolina.",
